<figure class="access-figure" data-context aria-labelledby="context-caption">
 <figcaption id="context-caption"><span class="figure-number">Figure 3</span> The same connection, another request</figcaption>
 <div class="access-scene">
  <p class="stage-label" data-context-stage data-live>1. Set up the first request</p>
  <div class="context-flow"><div><span>Request’s authorised tenant</span><strong data-request data-live>10</strong></div><div><span>Connection’s tenant context</span><strong data-tenant-context data-live>10</strong><code>shop_runtime</code></div><div><span>Rows returned by policy</span><strong data-context-result data-live>Not queried</strong></div></div>
  <p class="context-event" data-event data-live>BEGIN → set context 10</p>
  <p class="access-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">A request authorised for tenant 10 borrows a connection. The service starts a transaction and sets tenant context to 10 before its first data query.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="access-controls">
  <label>Context lifetime <select data-context-choice><option value="transaction">Transaction only</option><option value="session">Retained in session</option></select></label>
  <div class="playback" role="group" aria-label="Figure 3 playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span></div>
  <div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="access-caption">A conceptual connection-reuse sequence. At step 4, the application has accepted a different tenant but omitted context setup. A transaction-scoped value leaves this request with no rows; a retained session value exposes the previous tenant’s rows.</p>
 <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>Request 10 sets context 10 and reads Mina, Tariq and Edda. After the transaction, transaction-only context is absent; session context remains 10. A later tenant-20 request that omits setup therefore receives no rows with transaction-only context, or tenant 10’s rows with retained context. Correctly setting context 20 makes the policy return Rowan. The model assumes that missing context matches no rows and that the session has no older tenant value to restore.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import { contextSteps } from './facts.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-context]').forEach(root=>{
  const choice=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-context-choice]')!;
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:step=>{
   const retained=choice.value==='session';
   const values=[['10','10','Not queried','BEGIN → set context 10'],['10','10','Mina, Tariq, Edda','SELECT customers'],['None',retained?'10':'Absent','No query','COMMIT → return connection'],['20',retained?'10':'Absent',retained?'Mina, Tariq, Edda':'No rows','BUG: query before setting context'],['20','20','Rowan','BEGIN → set context 20 → query']];
   ['[data-request]','[data-tenant-context]','[data-context-result]','[data-event]'].forEach((s,i)=>root.querySelector(s)!.textContent=values[step][i]);
   root.querySelector('[data-context-stage]')!.textContent=['1. Set up the first request','2. Read tenant 10','3. End the transaction','4. Reuse without setup','5. Set up the next request'][step];
   root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=contextSteps[step]+(step===3?(retained?' The policy still sees 10, so it exposes tenant 10 to this tenant-20 request.':' With no matching context, the policy returns no rows. The request has failed safely, but still needs its setup bug fixed.'):'');
   root.querySelector('.context-flow')!.setAttribute('data-warning',String(step===3&&retained));
  }}); choice.addEventListener('change',player.render);
 });
</script>
